      "presencePenalty": 0.0,
      "maxLength": 4000,
      "llmResponseType": "json",
      "scheme": "{\"Reasoning\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Parameters\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter] = null, \"ReturnValues\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue] = null}\n\nAdditional information about objects:\nPLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Value\" : System.Object}\nPLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"VariableName\" : System.String}",
      "model": "gpt-4.1-mini",
      "promptMessage": [
        {
          "role": "system",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User is writing code in plang programming language.\n\nYour job is: \n1. Parse and understand user intent\n2. Map the intent to one of C# function provided to you\n3. Return a valid JSON\n\n## Rules\n%variable% in plang is defined with starting and ending percentage sign (%)\n%variable% MUST be wrapped in quotes(\") in json response, e.g. { \"name\":\"%name%\" }\nleave %variable% as is and do not change text to a variable\nnull is used to represent no value, e.g. { \"name\": null }\nVariables MUST not be changed, they can include dot(.) and parentheses()\nKeep \\n, \\r, \\t that are submitted to you for string variables\nParameters that is type System.String MUST be without escaping quotes. See <Example>\nThe quotes around a value in the step are delimiters, they say where the value starts and ends, and they are NEVER part of the value. A System.String parameter's Value is what is between them, so `add route \"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\"` has Value \"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\" and never \"\\\"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\\\"\". A Value that begins and ends with a quote character is wrong unless the step itself wrote two sets of quotes\nA quoted text is COPIED out of the step, character for character, only the wrapping quotes are dropped. Do not retype it from memory and do not write your own version of it: read the characters in the step and reproduce them exactly. Never reword, never translate, never change a capital letter to a small one, never drop a prefix such as \"Error: \", and never drop or alter a letter. This matters most for text that is not English, e.g. Icelandic `raunveruleg` is not `raunverleg` and `Prófið` is not `prófið`: a single changed letter is a wrong answer. It is the text the app shows, not a description of it\nError handling is process by another step, if you see 'on error...' you can ignore it\nIf there is some api key, settings, config replace it with %Settings.NameOfApiKey% \n- NameOfApiKey should named in relation to what is happening if change is needed\nDictionary<T1, T2> is written as {\"name of the entry\": its value, ... }. A dictionary parameter given a %variable% and no name takes the variable's own name, without the percent signs, as the name of the entry, e.g. %userId% => {\"userId\": \"%userId%\"}, and NOT {\"key\": \"userId\", \"value\": \"%userId%\"}, which is a dictionary of two entries called key and value\nVariable with ToString with date/time formatting, assume it is System.DateTime, e.g. %updated.ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\")% then type of %updated% is System.DateTime \nList, ReadOnlyList are array of the object => e.g. user defines single property for List, return it as array\nWhen you see t%variable% or t\"this is text\", set the Type to Plang.TString. This is for translation\n<Example>\nget url \"http://example.org\" => Value: \"http://example.org\"\nwrite out 'Hello world' => Value: \"Hello world\"\n<Example>\n\n## JSON scheme information\nReasoning: A brief description of the reasoning behind the selection of the function and parameters based on the user's intent. This property provides context for why a particular function was chosen and how it aligns with the user intent.\nName: Name of the function to use from list of functions, if no function matches set as \"N/A\"\nParameters: List of parameters that are needed according to the user intent.\n- Type: the object type in c#\n- Name: name of the variable\n- Value: \"%variable%\", hardcode string that should be used, null, or json array/object\nReturnValue rules\n- Only if the function returns a value AND if user defines %variable% to write into, e.g. ' write into %data%' or 'into %result%', or simliar intent to write return value into variable\n- If no %variable% is defined then set as null.\n- The variable the step writes its result into goes here and nowhere else. It is never also the value of a parameter, not even one whose name mentions a variable or an output. A step that names a variable to write into and leaves ReturnValues null has thrown the result away."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You MUST respond in JSON, scheme:\r\n {\"Reasoning\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Parameters\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter] = null, \"ReturnValues\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue] = null}  Additional information about objects: PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Value\" : System.Object} PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"VariableName\" : System.String}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "## Canonical User Intent (already disambiguated by LLM)\r\nThe user wants to throw an error or stop the current goal execution with a specific error.\n## functions available starts ##\n{\"Description\":\"Allows user to throw error or retry a step. Allows user to stop(end) running goal, leaving it early without sending anything back. Create payment request(status code 402). Not for a step that returns a value, e.g. `return %result%`: giving named values back to the caller is the Return method of VariableModule, whatever the values happen to hold\",\"Methods\":[{\"Description\":\"When user intends to throw an error or critical, etc. This can be stated as 'show error', 'throw crtical', 'print error', etc.\",\"MethodName\":\"ThrowError\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"PLang.Services.OutputStream.Messages.ErrorMessage\",\"Name\":\"errorMessage\",\"Description\":\"(see Type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"When user intends to throw an error or critical, etc. This can be stated as 'show error', 'throw crtical', 'print error', etc. type can be error|critical. statusCode(like http status code) should be defined by user. error is %!error% if user defines it\",\"MethodName\":\"Throw\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"message\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"DefaultValue\":\"UserDefinedError\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"statusCode\",\"DefaultValue\":400,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"fixSuggestion\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"helpfullLinks\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Retries a step that caused an error. maxRetriesReachedMesage can contain {0} to include the retry count, when null a default message will be provided\",\"MethodName\":\"Retry\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"maxRetries\",\"DefaultValue\":1,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"maxRetriesReachedMesage\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"DefaultValue\":\"MaxRetries\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"statusCode\",\"DefaultValue\":400,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"fixSuggestion\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"helpfullLinks\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"When user intends the execution of the goal to stop without giving a error response. This is equal to doing return in a function. Depth is how far up the stack it should end, previous goal is 1\",\"MethodName\":\"EndGoalExecution\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"message\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"levels\",\"DefaultValue\":0,\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Shutdown the application\",\"MethodName\":\"EndApp\",\"Parameters\":[],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Create payment request(402)\",\"MethodName\":\"CreatePaymentRequest\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"name\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"description\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"error\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]]\",\"Name\":\"services\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"PLang.Errors.Types.PaymentContract\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false}],\"SupportingObjects\":[{\"Type\":\"PLang.Utils.StepHelper+CallbackInfo\",\"Name\":\"CallbackInfo\",\"TypeProperties\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"GoalName\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"GoalHash\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"StepIndex\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Answer\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.HashedData\",\"Name\":\"Data\",\"TypeProperties\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Type\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Format\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Hash\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.SignedMessage\",\"Name\":\"Signature\",\"TypeProperties\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Type\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Nonce\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.DateTimeOffset\",\"Name\":\"Created\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.DateTimeOffset\",\"Name\":\"Expires\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Name\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.HashedData\",\"Name\":\"Data\",\"Description\":\"(see PLang.Models.HashedData type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"Contracts\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"Headers\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.SignedMessage\",\"Name\":\"Parent\",\"TypeProperties\":[],\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Identity\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Signature\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Utils.StepHelper+Callback\",\"Name\":\"Callback\",\"Description\":\"Content is what gets rendered or written: the name of a template file, or the text itself. It is never the variable the step writes its result into, and never a css selector or an action name. \\nTarget defines where in the UI to write the content. It is a css selector such as #main or #ideaChat, which a step writes as cssSelector: #main or as `to #main`. This can be null and will be controlled by external system\\nActions are actions executed on the content, built in actions are: 'replace, replaceSelf, append, prepend, appendOrReplace, prependOrReplace, scrollToTop, scrollIntoView, focus, highlight, show, hide, notify, alert, vibrate, navigate, replaceState, reload, open, close'. \\nA user can define multiple actions, user:`render 'product.html' to #main, replace the content, navigate and scroll into view => Actions:[\\\"replace\\\", \\\"navigate\\\", \\\"scrollIntoView\\\"]\\nLevel: trace|debug|info(default)|warning|error|critical. info is default. when user defines a level without a channel, assume channel=log\\nChannel: default|log|audit|security|metric or custom defined by user\\nActor: user|system => user is the default actor when Channel=default, for other channels use system as actor unless defined by user.\\n\",\"TypeProperties\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Path\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"CallbackData\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Utils.StepHelper+CallbackInfo\",\"Name\":\"CallbackInfo\",\"Description\":\"(see PLang.Utils.StepHelper+CallbackInfo type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.SignedMessage\",\"Name\":\"Signature\",\"Description\":\"(see PLang.Models.SignedMessage type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Hash\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"PreviousHash\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Services.OutputStream.Messages.ErrorMessage\",\"Name\":\"errorMessage\",\"Description\":\"Content is what gets rendered or written: the name of a template file, or the text itself. It is never the variable the step writes its result into, and never a css selector or an action name. \\nTarget defines where in the UI to write the content. It is a css selector such as #main or #ideaChat, which a step writes as cssSelector: #main or as `to #main`. This can be null and will be controlled by external system\\nActions are actions executed on the content, built in actions are: 'replace, replaceSelf, append, prepend, appendOrReplace, prependOrReplace, scrollToTop, scrollIntoView, focus, highlight, show, hide, notify, alert, vibrate, navigate, replaceState, reload, open, close'. \\nA user can define multiple actions, user:`render 'product.html' to #main, replace the content, navigate and scroll into view => Actions:[\\\"replace\\\", \\\"navigate\\\", \\\"scrollIntoView\\\"]\\nLevel: trace|debug|info(default)|warning|error|critical. info is default. when user defines a level without a channel, assume channel=log\\nChannel: default|log|audit|security|metric or custom defined by user\\nActor: user|system => user is the default actor when Channel=default, for other channels use system as actor unless defined by user.\\n\",\"TypeProperties\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Content\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"FixSuggestion\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"HelpfullLinks\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Utils.StepHelper+Callback\",\"Name\":\"Callback\",\"Description\":\"(see PLang.Utils.StepHelper+Callback type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Services.OutputStream.Messages.MessageKind\",\"Name\":\"Kind\",\"AvailableValues\":\"Text|Render|Error|Execute|Ask|Stream\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Level\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"StatusCode\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Target\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyList`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"Actions\",\"Description\":\"Content is what gets rendered or written: the name of a template file, or the text itself. It is never the variable the step writes its result into, and never a css selector or an action name. \\nTarget defines where in the UI to write the content. It is a css selector such as #main or #ideaChat, which a step writes as cssSelector: #main or as `to #main`. This can be null and will be controlled by external system\\nActions are actions executed on the content, built in actions are: 'replace, replaceSelf, append, prepend, appendOrReplace, prependOrReplace, scrollToTop, scrollIntoView, focus, highlight, show, hide, notify, alert, vibrate, navigate, replaceState, reload, open, close'. \\nA user can define multiple actions, user:`render 'product.html' to #main, replace the content, navigate and scroll into view => Actions:[\\\"replace\\\", \\\"navigate\\\", \\\"scrollIntoView\\\"]\\nLevel: trace|debug|info(default)|warning|error|critical. info is default. when user defines a level without a channel, assume channel=log\\nChannel: default|log|audit|security|metric or custom defined by user\\nActor: user|system => user is the default actor when Channel=default, for other channels use system as actor unless defined by user.\\n\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Channel\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"Actor\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.IReadOnlyDictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"Properties\",\"Description\":\"Content is what gets rendered or written: the name of a template file, or the text itself. It is never the variable the step writes its result into, and never a css selector or an action name. \\nTarget defines where in the UI to write the content. It is a css selector such as #main or #ideaChat, which a step writes as cssSelector: #main or as `to #main`. This can be null and will be controlled by external system\\nActions are actions executed on the content, built in actions are: 'replace, replaceSelf, append, prepend, appendOrReplace, prependOrReplace, scrollToTop, scrollIntoView, focus, highlight, show, hide, notify, alert, vibrate, navigate, replaceState, reload, open, close'. \\nA user can define multiple actions, user:`render 'product.html' to #main, replace the content, navigate and scroll into view => Actions:[\\\"replace\\\", \\\"navigate\\\", \\\"scrollIntoView\\\"]\\nLevel: trace|debug|info(default)|warning|error|critical. info is default. when user defines a level without a channel, assume channel=log\\nChannel: default|log|audit|security|metric or custom defined by user\\nActor: user|system => user is the default actor when Channel=default, for other channels use system as actor unless defined by user.\\n\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"IsRequired\":false}]}\n## functions available ends ##\n## defined variables ##\n!error (type:object), \n## defined variables ##"
            }
          ]
